{
  "schema": "dpa-review.adequacy-cases.v1",
  "note": "Written from the Official Journal snapshots in sources/oj before the rule code changed, and ported from fix/chapter-v-adequacy-model into the input shape of main. Each case quotes the provision it rests on; tests/test_adequacy.py checks that every quote occurs verbatim in the cited snapshot, that every input passes the input contract, and that check_transfers gives the expected status, severity and cited decision. An input is a fragment of a DPA description that the test adds to the smallest valid input. Status and severity follow the packet convention: PRESENT/LOW where the decision covers the transfer, MISSING/HIGH where no Chapter V basis is recorded, NEEDS_REVIEW/HIGH where an adequacy condition is unknown (owner answer of 10 November 2026). A case with an interpretation key rests on a reading of the decision that awaits lawyer review. Recipients are described by their facts only; no organisation is named.",
